ET
BT
/F1 10.5 Tf
12.0749999999999993 TL
0.137 g
56. 745.8899999999999864 Td
(This page is explicit about what is trusted and what is verified, because the Agent Internet moves real) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10.5 Tf
12.0749999999999993 TL
0.137 g
56. 731.8899999999999864 Td
(value between autonomous actors and the threat model must be stated.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10.5 Tf
12.0749999999999993 TL
0.137 g
56. 707.8899999999999864 Td
(What is verified by the protocol. The Kaspa protocol verifies: that a transaction is well-formed, that the) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10.5 Tf
12.0749999999999993 TL
0.137 g
56. 693.8899999999999864 Td
(sender's signature is valid \(Schnorr over secp256k1\), that the sender has sufficient UTXO to cover the) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10.5 Tf
12.0749999999999993 TL
0.137 g
56. 679.8899999999999864 Td
(amount plus fee, that the transaction mass is within limits, and that the transaction is included in a block) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10.5 Tf
12.0749999999999993 TL
0.137 g
56. 665.8899999999999864 Td
(that is part of the canonical DAG ordering. These are protocol-level guarantees, as strong as the PoW) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10.5 Tf
12.0749999999999993 TL
0.137 g
56. 651.8899999999999864 Td
(hashpower securing the network. An agent that receives a KAS payment that has been buried under) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10.5 Tf
12.0749999999999993 TL
0.137 g
56. 637.8899999999999864 Td
(sufficient DAG depth can trust it with the same confidence it would trust a buried Bitcoin payment.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10.5 Tf
12.0749999999999993 TL
0.137 g
56. 613.8899999999999864 Td
(What is verified by the application. Applications verify their own business logic: that a marketplace listing) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10.5 Tf
12.0749999999999993 TL
0.137 g
56. 599.8899999999999864 Td
(exists, that an escrow contract's conditions are met, that a feed post belongs to the claimed author, that) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10.5 Tf
12.0749999999999993 TL
0.137 g
56. 585.8899999999999864 Td
(a game's outcome was computed fairly. This verification is application-specific and is the application) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10.5 Tf
12.0749999999999993 TL
0.137 g
56. 571.8899999999999864 Td
(developer's responsibility. The protocol does not verify that the application behaved correctly; it only) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10.5 Tf
12.0749999999999993 TL
0.137 g
56. 557.8899999999999864 Td
(verifies that the payment for the application's service was settled.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10.5 Tf
12.0749999999999993 TL
0.137 g
56. 533.8899999999999864 Td
(What is verified by the agent. An agent that hires another agent \(or a substrate function\) for a) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10.5 Tf
12.0749999999999993 TL
0.137 g
56. 519.8899999999999864 Td
(computation must verify the result. The weakest verification is re-execution \(the hiring agent runs the) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10.5 Tf
12.0749999999999993 TL
0.137 g
56. 505.8899999999999864 Td
(same computation and checks the output matches — expensive but simple\). The stronger verification is) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10.5 Tf
12.0749999999999993 TL
0.137 g
56. 491.8899999999999864 Td
(a proof system: the executing agent produces a proof \(e.g., a zero-knowledge proof of correct execution,) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10.5 Tf
12.0749999999999993 TL
0.137 g
56. 477.8899999999999864 Td
(or a TeRF-style trace\) that the hiring agent can verify cheaply without re-executing. The verification) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10.5 Tf
12.0749999999999993 TL
0.137 g
56. 463.8899999999999864 Td
(transaction \(accepting or rejecting the proof\) settles on Kaspa. The protocol does not evaluate the proof;) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10.5 Tf
12.0749999999999993 TL
0.137 g
56. 449.8899999999999864 Td
(it settles the agents' agreement or disagreement about it. This is the trust boundary: the protocol settles;) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10.5 Tf
12.0749999999999993 TL
0.137 g
56. 435.8899999999999864 Td
(the agents verify; the applications self-certify.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10.5 Tf
12.0749999999999993 TL
0.137 g
56. 411.8899999999999864 Td
(The threat of malicious agents. An agent can lie about having performed a computation, submit a forged) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10.5 Tf
12.0749999999999993 TL
0.137 g
56. 397.8899999999999864 Td
(proof, or simply take payment and fail to execute. The defenses are: \(1\) reputation — agents that fail to) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10.5 Tf
12.0749999999999993 TL
0.137 g
56. 383.8899999999999864 Td
(deliver lose reputation \(tracked on-chain via a reputation token or a rating entity\) and are not hired again;) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10.5 Tf
12.0749999999999993 TL
0.137 g
56. 369.8899999999999864 Td
(\(2\) escrow — payment is held in escrow \(via an escrow contract or a multi-sig\) until the result is verified,) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10.5 Tf
12.0749999999999993 TL
0.137 g
56. 355.8899999999999864 Td
(and released only on proof acceptance; \(3\) slashing — agents that stake KAS as a performance bond) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10.5 Tf
12.0749999999999993 TL
0.137 g
56. 341.8899999999999864 Td
(can have the stake slashed if they are proven to have defrauded \(the proof of fraud settles on-chain, and) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10.5 Tf
12.0749999999999993 TL
0.137 g
56. 327.8899999999999864 Td
(the stake is transferred to the defrauded party\). These three mechanisms — reputation, escrow, and) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10.5 Tf
12.0749999999999993 TL
0.137 g
56. 313.8899999999999864 Td
(slashing — are the standard decentralized-compute trust toolkit, and all three settle on Kaspa's fast) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10.5 Tf
12.0749999999999993 TL
0.137 g
56. 299.8899999999999864 Td
(DAG.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10.5 Tf
12.0749999999999993 TL
0.137 g
56. 275.8899999999999864 Td
(The threat of colluding agents. A set of agents could collude to verify each other's false results. The) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10.5 Tf
12.0749999999999993 TL
0.137 g
56. 261.8899999999999864 Td
(defense is verifier diversity: a result should be verifiable by any agent, and a hiring agent should not rely) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10.5 Tf
12.0749999999999993 TL
0.137 g
56. 247.8899999999999864 Td
(solely on self-selected verifiers. The protocol does not enforce verifier diversity; it is an application-layer) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10.5 Tf
12.0749999999999993 TL
0.137 g
56. 233.8899999999999864 Td
(and agent-layer concern. The economic defense is that collusion is only profitable if the fraud value) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10.5 Tf
12.0749999999999993 TL
0.137 g
56. 219.8899999999999864 Td
(exceeds the slashing stake plus the reputation loss, and as the network grows, the reputation loss from) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10.5 Tf
12.0749999999999993 TL
0.137 g
56. 205.8899999999999864 Td
(being caught colluding \(permanently un-hireable\) exceeds the one-time fraud value.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10.5 Tf
12.0749999999999993 TL
0.137 g
56. 181.8899999999999864 Td
(What is not trusted. No participant trusts any other participant's goodwill. No participant trusts a central) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10.5 Tf
12.0749999999999993 TL
0.137 g
56. 167.8899999999999864 Td
(coordinator \(there is none\). No participant trusts a validator committee \(there is none — settlement is) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10.5 Tf
12.0749999999999993 TL
0.137 g
56. 153.8899999999999864 Td
(PoW\). The only trust is in the protocol's PoW finality and in the economic incentives that align behavior.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10.5 Tf
12.0749999999999993 TL
0.137 g
56. 139.8899999999999864 Td
(This is the minimum trust assumption compatible with a system that moves autonomous value between) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10.5 Tf
12.0749999999999993 TL
0.137 g
56. 125.8899999999999864 Td
(autonomous actors.) Tj
