(PAGE 13 — THE RELATIONSHIP TO EXISTING APPROACHES) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10.5 Tf
12.0749999999999993 TL
0.137 g
56. 745.8899999999999864 Td
(This page situates the thesis relative to the systems a knowledgeable reader will compare it to, to) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10.5 Tf
12.0749999999999993 TL
0.137 g
56. 731.8899999999999864 Td
(forestall the objection "isn't this just X?") Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10.5 Tf
12.0749999999999993 TL
0.137 g
56. 707.8899999999999864 Td
(vs. traditional supercomputing \(HPC clusters, national labs\). Traditional supercomputers are) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10.5 Tf
12.0749999999999993 TL
0.137 g
56. 693.8899999999999864 Td
(substrate-first: the interconnect, the scheduler, and the resource manager are built first, and applications) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10.5 Tf
12.0749999999999993 TL
0.137 g
56. 679.8899999999999864 Td
(are ported to them. They achieve extraordinary peak performance on tightly-coupled, pre-specified) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10.5 Tf
12.0749999999999993 TL
0.137 g
56. 665.8899999999999864 Td
(workloads \(fluid dynamics, molecular dynamics\). They are poor at heterogeneous, emergent,) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10.5 Tf
12.0749999999999993 TL
0.137 g
56. 651.8899999999999864 Td
(agent-driven workloads because their substrate was not derived from such workloads. TTT 3.0 is not a) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10.5 Tf
12.0749999999999993 TL
0.137 g
56. 637.8899999999999864 Td
(competitor to HPC for tightly-coupled simulation; it is a different category — a substrate for emergent,) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10.5 Tf
12.0749999999999993 TL
0.137 g
56. 623.8899999999999864 Td
(agent-driven, value-settled computation that no HPC center was built to serve.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10.5 Tf
12.0749999999999993 TL
0.137 g
56. 599.8899999999999864 Td
(vs. serverless computing \(AWS Lambda, Cloudflare Workers\). Serverless is substrate-first with a) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10.5 Tf
12.0749999999999993 TL
0.137 g
56. 585.8899999999999864 Td
(developer-friendly abstraction: write a function, pay per invocation. It is excellent for known, specified) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10.5 Tf
12.0749999999999993 TL
0.137 g
56. 571.8899999999999864 Td
(workloads. It does not derive its substrate from usage; it imposes a fixed substrate \(the function) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10.5 Tf
12.0749999999999993 TL
0.137 g
56. 557.8899999999999864 Td
(invocation model\) and charges developers to fit their applications into it. Serverless also does not settle) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10.5 Tf
12.0749999999999993 TL
0.137 g
56. 543.8899999999999864 Td
(payments between autonomous agents — the billing is between the developer and the cloud provider,) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10.5 Tf
12.0749999999999993 TL
0.137 g
56. 529.8899999999999864 Td
(not between agents. TTT 3.0 differs in both the derivation order \(usage-first\) and the payment model) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10.5 Tf
12.0749999999999993 TL
0.137 g
56. 515.8899999999999864 Td
(\(agent-to-agent, on-chain\).) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10.5 Tf
12.0749999999999993 TL
0.137 g
56. 491.8899999999999864 Td
(vs. decentralized compute tokens \(Golem, Akash, Render, etc.\). These projects built compute) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10.5 Tf
12.0749999999999993 TL
0.137 g
56. 477.8899999999999864 Td
(marketplaces: providers offer compute, consumers pay in token. They are substrate-first in the sense) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10.5 Tf
12.0749999999999993 TL
0.137 g
56. 463.8899999999999864 Td
(that they specified the compute primitive \(a container, a job, a render\) before they had the applications) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10.5 Tf
12.0749999999999993 TL
0.137 g
56. 449.8899999999999864 Td
(to fill it. Most struggled with adoption because the compute primitive did not match what application) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10.5 Tf
12.0749999999999993 TL
0.137 g
56. 435.8899999999999864 Td
(developers wanted to build. They also largely used proof-of-stake or delegated consensus, not PoW, so) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10.5 Tf
12.0749999999999993 TL
0.137 g
56. 421.8899999999999864 Td
(their settlement finality is weaker \(committee-based, not hashpower-based\). TTT 3.0 differs in build) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10.5 Tf
12.0749999999999993 TL
0.137 g
56. 407.8899999999999864 Td
(order \(applications first\) and in settlement \(Kaspa PoW\).) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10.5 Tf
12.0749999999999993 TL
0.137 g
56. 383.8899999999999864 Td
(vs. AI agent frameworks \(AutoGPT, BabyAGI, LangChain agents\). These frameworks provide the agent) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10.5 Tf
12.0749999999999993 TL
0.137 g
56. 369.8899999999999864 Td
(runtime \(the plan-act loop\) but do not provide the application library, the payment rail, or the substrate.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10.5 Tf
12.0749999999999993 TL
0.137 g
56. 355.8899999999999864 Td
(They are tools for building agents, not systems in which agents operate a real economy. TTT 3.0's agent) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10.5 Tf
12.0749999999999993 TL
0.137 g
56. 341.8899999999999864 Td
(runtime draws on the same plan-act-verify pattern, but embeds it in a system where agents pay for and) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10.5 Tf
12.0749999999999993 TL
0.137 g
56. 327.8899999999999864 Td
(are paid for real computation on a real DAG. An agent framework without a settlement layer is a chatbot) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10.5 Tf
12.0749999999999993 TL
0.137 g
56. 313.8899999999999864 Td
(with extra steps; an agent framework with Kaspa settlement is a participant in an economy.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10.5 Tf
12.0749999999999993 TL
0.137 g
56. 289.8899999999999864 Td
(vs. the original "World Wide Web." The closest historical analogy is the Web itself. The Web was not) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10.5 Tf
12.0749999999999993 TL
0.137 g
56. 275.8899999999999864 Td
(built as a substrate for commerce; it was built as a document system. Commerce emerged from usage,) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10.5 Tf
12.0749999999999993 TL
0.137 g
56. 261.8899999999999864 Td
(and the infrastructure \(CDNs, payment gateways, ad networks\) was reverse-engineered from the usage) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10.5 Tf
12.0749999999999993 TL
0.137 g
56. 247.8899999999999864 Td
(patterns that emerged. TTT 3.0 claims the same dynamic at the compute layer: build the application) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10.5 Tf
12.0749999999999993 TL
0.137 g
56. 233.8899999999999864 Td
(layer \(the "documents"\), let agents generate the usage graph \(the "traffic"\), and reverse-engineer the) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10.5 Tf
12.0749999999999993 TL
0.137 g
56. 219.8899999999999864 Td
(compute substrate \(the "infrastructure"\) from it. The Agent Internet is to distributed supercomputing what) Tj
